request: Make the output easier to read.

governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" is too vague to turn into a testable contract. The output comes from format.formatTodo/formatList, and existing tests probably pin the current format, so any change could break them. Before changing behaviour I need a concrete target format.)
governor asks: I can change how the todo list looks, but "easier to read" could mean a few different things. Which of these do you want? (1) A status marker per item, e.g. "[ ]" for open and "[x]" for done. (2) IDs, titles and due dates lined up in columns. (3) Due dates shown a different way, e.g. "(due 2024-05-01)", or overdue items highlighted. (4) A header or summary line, e.g. "3 todos, 1 done". (5) A clear message when the list is empty. (6) ANSI colours. (7) Something else. If you can, please paste an example of how a list with 2–3 todos (one done, one with a due date) should look. Should the add/complete confirmation messages change too, or only the list output?

